'''Sanyan International Airport''' ({{Langx|kz|ߛߊߣߦߊ߲ ߊߜߓߊߜߋߘߋ ߏߝߎߙߎߝߎ ߊߜߓߊߦߋ|Sànyán Gbàgede Òfúrufú Àgbáyé}}), is an [[W:International airport|international airport]] in the [[W:City-state|city-state]] of [[Sanyan]], situated at the eastern end of [[Owusuwusu|Owúsúwusù]] and neighboring waters which opened for commercial operations on 15 October 1989, taking over all services from the aging [[Joloyema Airport]]. Joloyema Airport was subsequently [[W:Land recycling|demolished and recycled]] into residential development.

Since then, the airport has been a common transfer point for people traveling across the Northern Hemisphere, as well as a passenger hub for destinations in mainland Kaftia and [[Abyala]]. During 2022, the airport handled 3 million passengers and 220,000 tonnes of cargo. In 2017 the number of passengers had increased to 7,165,803, which is more than the 6 million passengers per year the terminal was originally designed for.

